 property=\"og:title\" content=\"Tafsir of An-Naas 114:1 — by Ibn Taymiyyah and Ibn al-Qayyim\">\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Say, &quot;I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind,\">\n<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#1f4d3a\">\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/og.png\">\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\">\n<script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/en/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Surah An-Naas\", \"item\": \"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/en/surah/114.html\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Verse 1\", \"item\": \"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/en/ayah/114-1.html\"}]}</script>\n<link rel=\"icon\" href=\"/icon.svg\" type=\"image/svg+xml\">\n<link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\">\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Amiri+Quran&family=Amiri:wght@400;700&family=Noto+Naskh+Arabic:wght@400;600&display=swap\">\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/theme.css\">\n<style>body{font-family:system-ui,\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif;color:var(--ink);padding:20px 16px 48px;line-height:1.6}.tr{font-size:17px;line-height:1.8;margin:0}.cr{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)}.ar{direction:rtl;text-align:right}</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<main class=\"sp\"><nav class=\"crumbs\"><a href=\"/en/\">Home</a> › <a href=\"/en/surah/114.html\">Surah An-Naas</a> › Verse 1</nav><h1>Tafsir of Surah An-Naas 114:1</h1><p class=\"vt ar\" lang=\"ar\">﴿بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ قُلْ أَعُوذُ بِرَبِّ النَّاسِ﴾</p><section><h3>Translation of the meaning</h3><p class=\"tr\">Say, &quot;I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind,</p><span class=\"cr\" dir=\"ltr\">English Translation - Noor International Center — v1.1.2 · QuranEnc.com</span></section><p class=\"cr\">The words of the two imams are given in their original Arabic, verbatim, with references.</p><section><h2>Shaykh al-Islam Ibn Taymiyyah</h2><blockquote class=\"ar\" lang=\"ar\">فإن الوسواس أصل كل كفر وفسوق وعصيان فهو أصل الشر كله<cite>«مجموع الفتاوى» 17/518</cite></blockquote><blockquote class=\"ar\" lang=\"ar\">فأي ناس ليس الله ربهم؟ أم ليس ملكهم؟ أم ليس إلههم؟<cite>«مجموع الفتاوى» 6/444</cite></blockquote><blockquote class=\"ar\" lang=\"ar\">والربوبية تستلزم الإلهية؛ فإن أحدهما إذا تضمن الآخر عند الانفراد لم يمنع أن يختص معناه عند الاقتران،<cite>«الفتاوى الكبرى لابن تيمية» 5/252</cite></blockquote></section><section><h2>Imam Ibn al-Qayyim</h2><blockquote class=\"ar\" lang=\"ar\">فذكر ربوبيته للناس وملكه إياهم وإلهيته لهم<cite>«بدائع الفوائد» 2/247</cite></blockquote><blockquote class=\"ar\" lang=\"ar\">وإذا كان وحده هو ربنا ومالكنا وإلهنا فلا مفزع لنا في الشدائد سواه<cite>«بدائع الفوائد» 2/248</cite></blockquote></section><a class=\"btn pri open\" href=\"/tafsir.html?lang=en#s114a1\">Open in the interactive tafsir (full texts)</a><div class=\"pn\"><span></span><a href=\"/en/ayah/114-4.html\">Next verse (114:4)</a></div></main><footer class=\"site-foot\"><span>Tafsir al-Shaykhayn · <a href=\"/en/\">Home</a> · <a href=\"/about.html\">About the project</a> · <a href=\"/privacy.html\">Privacy &amp; terms</a></span><a href=\"https://doersadv.com\" rel=\"noopener\" dir=\"ltr\">Developed by Doers</a></footer>\n</body>\n</html>\n","ayah/114-4.html":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Tafsir of An-Naas 114:4 — by Ibn Taymiyyah and Ibn al-Qayyim</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"From the evil of the retreating whisperer -\">\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/en/ayah/114-4.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"ar\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/ayah/114-4.html\">\n<link rel=\"alter